# --- GOLDEN TEST FIXTURE ---
# resetMode=loadvm : the guest boots a READ-ONLY live ISO, so the snapshot
# "golden" (live RAM + disk) lives in ravynos-golden.qcow2, an otherwise unused
# carrier disk that exists only to hold it. OVMF_VARS.qcow2 carries the tag too
# (0 B of vmstate) and must be rolled back with it -- the pair is atomic.
SH_RESET_MODE=loadvm
SH_GOLDEN_SNAPSHOT=golden
SH_GOLDEN_DISKS=ravynos-golden.qcow2 OVMF_VARS.qcow2
# Fixture: the ravynOS 0.6.1 "Hyperpop Hyena" live desktop, logged in as
# liveuser, at 1280x800. Global menu bar with the raven glyph and the clock, the
# Zakim-bridge wallpaper drawn by Dock.app, and the Dock itself (Terminal,
# Install, Trash). No windows open. See docs/guests/ravynos.md.
#
# THE MENU-BAR CLOCK TICKS. This station has no idle-deterministic frame: the
# clock repaints once a minute and there is no setting in 0.6.x to hide it.
# Compare golden captures at a fixed machine instant instead --
#   stop ; loadvm golden ; stop ; screendump out.ppm ; cont
# -- which is what proved this station's restore byte-exact.
